    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "build: pass hardening flags to secp256k1",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The secp256k1 subtree is built without our hardening flags. They are on `core_interface`, and `cmake/secp256k1.cmake` passes the subtree only the sanitizer and `APPEND_*` flags, so unless the compiler enables them by default its objects miss FORTIFY, the stack protector, stack clash protection and control flow protection. On aarch64 Ubuntu 26.04 with GCC 15 this also costs the whole binary its control flow property: master's `bitcoind` has no `AArch64 feature` note, and the three secp256k1 objects are the only ones in the build tree without it.\n\nThis PR moves the flags back to a `hardening_interface` library, which `core_interface` links; the `CMakeLists.txt` change is a revert of 77e553ab6a plus one comment. `cmake/secp256k1.cmake` then passes them to the subtree the same way as `sanitize_interface`. With it, the same build shows `AArch64 feature: BTI, PAC, GCS` on `bitcoind`. It does not fix #30677 on its own: the depends libraries are still built without `-fcf-protection`, which #30685 tried to change.\n",
